    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nwhen i try to rename a file to be inside a folder, it throws an error.\r\n\r\n![rename](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/9551316/97af15e7-7d4c-40d2-b8a2-641332d19489)\r\n\r\n(Sometimes don't throw error)\r\n\r\nwhen throws:\r\n\r\n```\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: ...vio/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1208: Invalid window id: 1002\r\nstack traceback:\r\n\t[C]: in function 'nvim_win_get_buf'\r\n\t...vio/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1208: in function 'explorer_refresh'\r\n\t...vio/.local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1713: in function ''\r\n\tvim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\r\n```\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open mini.files\r\n2. Rename a file to be inside a folder, like: \"myfile.rb\" -> \"folder/myfile.rb\"\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nCreate a folder and put the file inside\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nnothing happens",
